One thing I've noticed in roguelikes is that many of them (including
Tales of Middle Earth, Omega and Ancient Domains of Mystery) have some
kind of ASCII art title screen. Well, I've prepared a patch that adds
one for TTY, X11 and Amiga NetHack.

What is it? Just an ASCII rendition of the title "NetHack" in a
pseudo-gothic style resembling the one on the main page of
www.nethack.org .

Notes:
* Doesn't appear in Windows versions yet!
* The "Shall I pick a character's race, role, gender and alignment for
you?" question is, undeniably, pushed to the very bottom line.

